## 1. QA Decision

Decision: pass

The sole QA decision owner is qa-gate. At Run revision 30, current CD+Tests, TP Review, Clean Implementation Review and mandatory CR are registered done and source-associated. Exact approved UR/PRD/SD/TP and source-revision history remain intact. All eight PRD criteria and 24 mapped technical scenarios are sufficiently evidenced; no applicable open or invalid normalized finding remains. The explicit direct human authorization for the post-qualification test-only correction is attributed and assessed rather than represented as an inferred TP approval or an applied source revision.

## 2. TP Coverage

- delivered_result: The existing MCP inspection contract exposes all 14 parameters and 11 operations in the named Codex renderer while retaining original input acceptance. Explicitly bound reads can return complete sequential read arguments from canonical catalog/command owners without changing report truth, document identity or approval authority. Two genuine normal T7 sessions on the unchanged final runtime each record exactly one intended UR approval in four MCP calls with zero SDK/other errors. The unsupported-platform negative test now checks the actual stderr stream and passes alongside the full synthetic macOS guard suite.

TP_REVIEW.md evaluates all 11 tasks and their AC evidence individually. Its fully_done result is explicitly limited to the current phase: T-REVIEW supplies current review evidence and T-CLOSE reconciles scope/accounting. Later human QA/UAT/OR decisions are pending, not counted as already approved. AC-001 through AC-008 are done at the approved boundary with high evidence confidence. No P0/P1 gap or missing approved criterion was found; priorities were not invented.

The single out-of-frozen-plan change follows the user's explicit instruction "Fix ist ohne agdf zu nutzen", after native qualification completed. DIRECT_FIX_AUTHORIZATION_04.md preserves the direct scope and later reconciliation instruction. The prior TP source-revision preview remains unapplied; all approved source bytes remain unchanged. This narrow test-only correction changes neither runtime nor acceptance, task/audit, guard protection, session allowance or MCP/Copilot limits.

